tion":"Tri = three."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-8ec66b7776f5a761","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A square has how many corners (vertices)?","options":["3","5","6","4"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Square."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-b07024757a46180a","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A shape with 4 equal sides and 4 right angles is a:","options":["Rectangle","Square","Triangle","Circle"],"correctIndex":1,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Square."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-a90677dc8a4f4b8f","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A circle has how many corners?","options":["1","2","4","0"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"A circle has no corners."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-944b04a8900e97a4","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A shape with 6 sides is called a:","options":["Pentagon","Octagon","Square","Hexagon"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Hexa = six."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-6e3f5f9b2e43be06","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A ball is shaped like a:","options":["Cube","Cylinder","Sphere","Cone"],"correctIndex":2,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Sphere."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-fd45be75bf9bb9a0","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"An ice-cream cone is shaped like a:","options":["Cone","Cube","Sphere","Cylinder"],"correctIndex":0,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Cone."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-2742313a006d1163","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A dice is shaped like a:","options":["Sphere","Cone","Cylinder","Cube"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Cube."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-a311acb9c02088d7","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A straight line has how many end points?","options":["None (it goes on forever)","One","Two","Three"],"correctIndex":0,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Line has no end points."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-fb3266be69a6b281","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A line segment has how many end points?","options":["One","None","Three","Two"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Segment."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-0a1ec3dfd71dca44","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A ray has how many end points?","options":["Two","None","One","Three"],"correctIndex":2,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Ray."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-01c58e696ea4dfd8","chapterId":"el-b47-c6","topicId":"el-b47-t2520-0","type":"mcq","text":"A right angle measures:","options":["180°","45°","360°","90°"],"correctIndex":3,"page":137,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Right angle."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-fd8643bc25e08ab4","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"Information collected in the form of numbers is called:","options":["Graph","Table","Picture","Data"],"correctIndex":3,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Data."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-0876789a050e8927","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"A graph that uses pictures to show data is called a:","options":["Bar graph","Line graph","Pie chart","Pictograph"],"correctIndex":3,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Pictograph."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-77c6c8bcc79ec9b3","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"A graph that uses bars to show data is called a:","options":["Pictograph","Bar graph","Pie chart","Map"],"correctIndex":1,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Bar graph."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-63a24a4cec561e06","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"Tally marks (four lines with one line across) represent:","options":["5","4","6","10"],"correctIndex":0,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Group of five."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-aca3314cffadf979","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"In a pictograph, if one picture = 2 children, then 4 pictures =","options":["8 children","4 children","6 children","2 children"],"correctIndex":0,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"4 × 2."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-3626f7d714ce5ada","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"In a bar graph, the tallest bar shows the:","options":["Smallest value","Average","Greatest value","Total only"],"correctIndex":2,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Tallest = most."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-bd71bd60b84bd54f","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"Data arranged in rows and columns is called a:","options":["Graph","Picture","Table","Map"],"correctIndex":2,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Table."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-50abe7d0af24d50f","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"To record data quickly we use:","options":["Fractions","Tally marks","Clocks","Rulers"],"correctIndex":1,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Tally."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-4fa737e95e35c5c4","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"If 5 children like mango and 3 like apple, how many more like mango?","options":["8","2","3","5"],"correctIndex":1,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"5 − 3."},{"id":"el-b47-xelq-1a4c8bf69aacb9b9","chapterId":"el-b47-c7","topicId":"el-b47-t2533-0","type":"mcq","text":"If 5 children like mango and 3 like apple, how many in all?","options":["2","15","8","5"],"correctIndex":2,"page":162,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"5 + 3."}]}